# DNS bad expand
#
# This is testing Exim's code handling awkward implementations of the
# resolver library, where issues have turned up in the past.
# We use a custom psuedo-type for DNS enquries done using dnsdb lookups,
# which bypass the dn_expand() function. This lets us feed the datastream
# for our processing after that call, which has to undo the coding of bytes
# having a topbit set in the wire packet [that coding being done by
# dn_expand()].
#
# We need a working dir for fakens that is both
# user- and exim-writable.  spool is not user-w and DIR might not be exim-w.
# The dirname is coded in fakens also.
sudo rm -fr DIR/tmp
mkdir DIR/tmp
sudo chmod 777 DIR/tmp
#
#
dns
